      "question": "My manager wants a quick look at the oil condition on Transformer 1 at site MAIN. From the latest reading and the stats over the full available window, give me dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and say whether any of them moved in a direction that points to moisture ingress, air ingress or oil ageing. Rank the three concerns from most to least supported by the data. Don't use the combustible gases for this. If dielectric_rigidity or interfacial_v has no data, say so and base the ranking on oxygen and nitrogen only.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 \u2014 MAIN**  \nFull available window: **15\u201319 January 2024**, five readings each; latest: **19 January 2024, 00:00 UTC**. These are historical, not current-condition readings. Units were not supplied.\n\n| Parameter | Latest | Mean | Min\u2013max | Std. dev. | First\u2192latest change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| dielectric_rigidity | 55 | 54.6 | 53\u201356 | 1.02 | 0 |\n| interfacial_v | 45 | 45 | 44\u201346 | 0.63 | 0 |\n| oxygen | 5,850 | 5,822 | 5,700\u20135,900 | 68.82 | \u221210 |\n| nitrogen | 27,850 | 27,868.4 | 27,700\u201328,000 | 103.32 | +8 |\n| dbds | 19 | 19 | 18\u201320 | 0.63 | 0 |\n\n**Concern ranking: no defensible separation\u2014all three have weak or no sustained support.**\n\n1. **Moisture ingress \u2014 tied:** dielectric_rigidity briefly declined, a potentially consistent direction, but recovered; no net deterioration.\n1. **Oil ageing \u2014 tied:** interfacial_v briefly declined but recovered; no sustained decline. DBDS is unchanged overall and is principally a corrosive-sulfur indicator, not proof of ageing.\n1. **Air ingress \u2014 tied:** oxygen and nitrogen fluctuate without a sustained joint increase; their net changes are negligible and opposite.\n\nA strict most-to-least ordering would overstate these five readings. No combustible gases were used.",
